; Runtime errors of exceptions (--mode=objfpc): unhandled exceptions report
; their class, where they were raised and (Exception) their message; finally
; parts run before; raising nil is an error. Exit status 2. Integer
; division by zero raises EDivByZero (as in Free Pascal with SysUtils). An
; exception raised `at` an address is reported at it (as by Free Pascal),
; re-raised too.
; RUN: %p3 --mode=objfpc %S/Inputs/exceptions/rterrors.pas -o %t
; RUN: not %t exception 2>&1 | FileCheck --check-prefix=EXC %s
; EXC: Runtime error: unhandled exception Exception at {{.*}}rterrors.pas:22:5: boom
; RUN: not %t subclass 2>&1 | FileCheck --check-prefix=SUB %s
; SUB: finally runs first
; SUB-NEXT: Runtime error: unhandled exception EParse at {{.*}}rterrors.pas:13:5: bad token
; RUN: not %t plain 2>&1 | FileCheck --check-prefix=PLAIN %s
; PLAIN: Runtime error: unhandled exception TPlain at {{.*}}rterrors.pas:26:5{{$}}
; RUN: not %t nil 2>&1 | FileCheck --check-prefix=NIL %s
; NIL: Runtime error: 'raise' of a nil object at {{.*}}rterrors.pas:28:5
; A re-raise reports where the exception was first raised.
; RUN: not %t reraise 2>&1 | FileCheck --check-prefix=RERAISE %s
; RERAISE: handling first
; RERAISE-NEXT: Runtime error: unhandled exception EParse at {{.*}}rterrors.pas:31:7: first
; RUN: not %t unmatched 2>&1 | FileCheck --check-prefix=UNMATCHED %s
; UNMATCHED-NOT: not this
; UNMATCHED: Runtime error: unhandled exception TPlain at {{.*}}rterrors.pas:41:7
; RUN: %t none | FileCheck --check-prefix=NONE %s
; NONE: no error
; RUN: not %t divzero 2>&1 | FileCheck --check-prefix=DIVZERO %s
; DIVZERO: Runtime error: unhandled exception EDivByZero at {{.*}}rterrors.pas:46:23: Division by zero
; RUN: not %t at 2>&1 | FileCheck --check-prefix=AT %s
; AT: Runtime error: unhandled exception EParse at $0000000000000000: somewhere
; RUN: not %t reraiseat 2>&1 | FileCheck --check-prefix=RERAISEAT %s
; RERAISEAT: Runtime error: unhandled exception TPlain at $0000000000000000{{$}}
